# The Joint NSF/JISC International Digital Libraries Initiative [and] Personalized Information Environments: An Architecture for Customizable Access to Distributed Digital Libraries [and] A Report on the PEAK Experiment: Context and Design.

**Authors:** Wiseman, Norman, Rusbridge, Chris, Griffin, Stephen M., French, James C., Viles, Charles L., Bonn, Maria S., Lougee, Wendy P., MacKie-Mason, Jeffrey K., Riveros, Juan F.

## Abstract
Describes the joint NSF/JISC (National Science Foundation/UK Joint Information Systems Committee) International Digital Libraries Initiative. Discusses JISC funding criteria and procedures; personalized information environment (PIE), a conceptual architecture that allows unified, highly customizable access to distributed information resources; and Pricing Electronic Access to Knowledge (PEAK) a production service for electronic journal delivery and an opportunity for experimental pricing research. (AEF)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ613366

